so  [Music]  so i have some very exciting news for  you i'm back with a new film profile  made after the fujifilm maternal  simulation i've been very busy lately  and had very little time on hand but i  really wanted to make this video to  share with you these settings and how  you can get the same look using the  creative lut  also i will show you how to replicate  the cine steel 800 look so watch the  whole video to find out how  a little bit about the profile i'm  absolutely in love with the profile is  just gorgeous in terms of contrast and  how it renders colors i've been testing  it for a week or two in multiple  scenarios and lighting conditions and  it's just crazy good  last weekend actually i was at a party  and took a bunch of pictures with this  profile and the colors were so good that  i didn't even feel the need to edit them  so i just used the jpegs  it handles underexposing and  overexposing very very well with soft  gradations and pleasing colors  with most of my previous film profiles i  just like to keep the image a little bit  underexposed but with this profile being  so versatile i can just expose both ways  my only complaint with this profile is  that it shifts the yellow towards green  very much when overexposed and sometimes  it can give weird hues in the highlights  in some situations this is caused by the  c4 gamma generally that's the reason why  i usually avoided using destiny 4  because if you have watched my other  videos on film simulation for sony  cameras you can notice that none of the  film simulations that i've made is based  on 74 but this time i needed a more  contrasty look  also cine4 is probably the noisiest from  all cine gammas it's not a big issue if  you enjoy the grain but for the cleanest  image i will still use new one and  that's good to keep in mind as a  reference in this video the next iso  used was 2500 with a f 2.8 lens  many of you asked for a tutorial on how  to shoot these film profiles to get a  similar look i'm currently working on a  video explaining  general settings on how i shoot each  profile and i hope to finish it next  week subscribe to be notified about the  video when it comes out so now let's get  the cine steel look  this is the raw footage from the camera  shot on the alternate film profile and  grade it using the creative lut pack to  get even closer to the film look all you  have to do is choose the halation  strength from the creative lut folder  and apply it to the footage is that easy  to adjust the hilation just right click  on the node open the compound node and  on this layer adjust the red curve to  limit or extend the affected area you  can find these on my website linked down  below  you can see it looks really good out of  the camera and it's saving me a lot of  time that i would have spent on color  grading the way you can achieve this  cold cyan color is by shooting below  2500 kelvin  if you shoot sony you know the minimum  kelvin you can choose manually is 2500  but if you make a custom white balance  you can actually go even lower or higher  than the manual limits and i'll show you  exactly how you can do that  go into the color temperature menu you  can do that by going into the photo icon  at page 12 on the sony a7v but i  recommend assigning it to a button so  it's one step away in any given  situation i assign this menu to the  joystick just by clicking it so i can  easily access it at any time that is a  life saver in many occasions scroll down  to a custom balance press ok and now  find something yellow and fill the whole  screen with it and now press the middle  point  now the camera will try to correct the  yellow tint in the image and will  compensate by going under 2500 kelvin  save this color as a custom you can  create three of these custom colors and  trust me they are very helpful not only  for film colors but for day to day  shooting so use this function i've also  saved the creative lut for footage that  is shot on regular kelvin so you can  just drag and drop it on any footage  together with all the original grades  that i've used for the initial video  make sure to check them out and hit the  like button if you like this eterna  profile  to save this simulation just go into the  menu and find picture profile on the a7  iii is at page 12 in the image icon hit  ok press right to enter the menu and  there you can find all the settings that  you need the settings for this profile  are free but testing creating these  profiles and editing the videos take a  lot of time so please consider  supporting the channel by buying the  creative lots or by buying me a coffee i  appreciate your support and that's why  for the next month the less will be 50  off like subscribe if you haven't  already and thanks again for watching  see you soon

